~ start
Agnes: Hello, sister.  We finally have the chance to talk to each other again.
{{player_name}}: Hello, Agnes.  I want to say that I’m so unbelievably sorry for my horrible choices that I’ve made in the past.  I’ve heard that you're dying–I need to save you from this place!
Agnes:  That’s very kind of you, sister.  I thank you for your apology.  I think you have had a wonderful change of heart from how you acted in the mortal plane.  But it’s not enough to save me, not now–not with how closely I feel death's clutches.
{{player_name}}: Agnes, you’re fading away.  No!  What can I do!?
Agnes: And so are you, sister.  I need you to tell me specific details of both the event and your life which led us both down here.  Only when all is made clear can we put a stop to death’s attacks.
{{player_name}}: Ok, ok!  What do I have to say?
Agnes: I will ask you questions about the incident, ones that I haven’t made–they were given to me by fate, so I have to say each one.
Agnes: First!  What was the cause of your worsening mind before the car crash?  You were getting very angry, sister, because of all sorts of things, but what was the main cause?
- I had a heavy addiction.
	Agnes: Yes!  Those weird pills were clouding your mind.  Your friends were not good role models, but I always saw you messing yourself up each and every day because of your addiction.  You were really hurting the whole family, and I was incredibly worried and mad at you because of it.
	{{player_name}}: And I am very, very sorry for that!  I see now how wrong I’ve been.
	Agnes: I forgive you, but now I need to ask the second question! What is the special color I love so much?  I think it was the color of the night sky when you crashed the car.
- The color is midnight blue.
	Agnes: No, no! That’s wrong.  Oh… oh no!
	{{player_name}}: What is it Agnes, w-what can I do!?  
	Agnes: Nothing, sister, it’s all over!  I can’t hold to this form much longer… I feel the weight of death, it’s… it’s too heavy!
	Agnes: I… I’m free now.  A full spirit, free to wander this plane.  I’ll wait here for you, sister, and for mom and dad, too.
	{{player_name}}: No, I’ve failed you completely!  I just wanted to help save you from this fate.  I’ve killed you, this was my fault!  I’m so… so sorry, Agnes.
	Agnes: I forgive you, sister.  After what you have seen and what we have talked about, I fully forgive you.  I love you, sister.
	{{player_name}}: I love you, Agnes.
	Agnes: See you later, my sister.  Tell mom and dad that I love them too!
	{{player_name}}: I will!  Goodbye!
=> END

- The color is indigo.
	Agnes: Yes, yes!  I love indigo, it is so beautiful.  I’m glad that even before the bad crash, I got to see my favorite color in the sky.
	{{player_name}}: I am getting very, very worried, Agnes!  I must free you.   What’s the next question?
	Agnes: One more, sister, only one more!  What is the reason I am here but still alive, and the reason that you are visiting me?
	- You are being supernaturally held in limbo, so that I can save you by destroying my bad habits.
		Agnes: No, no! That’s wrong.  Oh… oh no!
